# auto.network — public front door vhost (bead auto-9q7a5).
#
# Reverse-proxies the bare apex to the registry service on loopback — the SAME
# uvicorn process (127.0.0.1:8477) that already answers registry.auto.network
# and relay.auto.network. The apex is where the agent-first /install primer and
# /healthz live for a human or agent who types just "auto.network".
#
# ROUTING ONLY. This vhost does not, and must not, change the registry's
# --base-url (https://relay.auto.network in autonomy-registry.service): newly
# minted share links keep issuing on relay.auto.network. Do not add a base-url
# override here or in the unit — the hostname split is deliberate:
#   auto.network          → public front door + /install
#   registry.auto.network → registry/control API compatibility
#   relay.auto.network    → issued share links + viewer WebSockets
#
# TLS: omitted on purpose. Caddy's automatic HTTPS mints and renews the
# Let's Encrypt certificate for auto.network. That requires auto.network to
# ALREADY resolve to this box (5.161.219.195) over HTTP-01 — deploy the apex A
# record FIRST (add-apex-a-record.sh), let it propagate, THEN install this vhost.
auto.network {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8477
}
